# L5 fix (31.anaysis.md): pinned SHA256 checksums for the third-party
# binaries fetched by infra/terraform/modules/asg/main.tf user_data.
#
# Format is the standard `sha256sum` output — one line per binary:
#   <sha256-hex>  <filename>
#
# The user_data grep-filters to the arch it needs, then feeds
# `sha256sum -c` in the download directory. If the arch line is missing
# the verify step logs SKIPPED and continues (fail-open for now so a
# fresh cut of the bundle doesn't brick a boot before the hash is
# populated — flip this to fail-closed once every arch is populated).
#
# populate with sha256sum from https://github.com/sigstore/cosign/releases/tag/v2.4.0
# and https://github.com/docker/compose/releases/tag/v2.27.0
#
# Example (fill in the real hex):
# <sha256>  cosign-linux-arm64
# <sha256>  cosign-linux-amd64
# <sha256>  docker-compose-linux-aarch64
# <sha256>  docker-compose-linux-x86_64
